  1480      @param[out] q    Location to store an updated value for p
  1481      @return The integer value, or zero if the type code was not valid.
  1482
  1483  Reads a one-byte type code from @p p, and uses it to decode an integer
  1484  value from the following bytes in @p p.
  1485
  1486  If the type is not one of BCF_BT_INT8, BCF_BT_INT16 or BCF_BT_INT32, zero
  1487  will be returned and @p *q will unchanged.  Otherwise, the integer value will
  1488  be returned and @p *q will be set to the memory location immediately following
  1489  the integer value.
  1490
  1491  Cautious callers can detect invalid type codes by checking that *q has
  1492  actually been updated.
  1493  */
  1494  static inline int64_t bcf_dec_typed_int1(const uint8_t *p, uint8_t **q)
  1495  {
  1496      return bcf_dec_int1(p + 1, *p&0xf, q);
